    },
    {
      "doc_type": "data_dictionary",
      "year": 2026,
      "title": "Data Governance | Saint Mary's College",
      "url": "https://www.stmarys-ca.edu/offices-services/academic-affairs/institutional-and-educational-effectiveness/data-governance",
      "summary": "The Data Governance page of Saint Mary's College of California details the institution's planned strategies for managing data through policies, practices and operations, aiming to support evidence-based decision making. The college-wide data strategies facilitate a comprehensive system for data management, including collection, pathways, integration, analysis, and distribution of data. The Data Governance Committee is responsible for transforming data into a strategic asset by establishing data definitions, maintaining data security, and fostering continuous improvement. This page includes information about their organizational structure, roles of committee members, data access regulations, and policies governing data integrity and security. Additionally, it introduces the data dictionary process and various data reports and dashboards within the institutional framework.",
